<title>USA: Mercantile to split stock, buyback shares.</title>
<headline>Mercantile to split stock, buyback shares.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercantile Bancorp Inc, a $22.6 billion asset bank holding company, said Wednesday it declared a three-for-two stock split.</p>
<p>The company also said it plans to repurchase up to 3.75 million shares of its common stock to fund its amended stock incentive plan.  </p>
<p>Mercantile also declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.43 per share of common stock. The dividend is payable October 1, 1997 to shareholders of record as of September 10, 1997.</p>
<p>Mercantile shares rose 3-7/8 to 67-7/8 Wednesday.</p>
<p>	 ((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
